# Developer-stack configuration for compose.dev.yml.
#
# Copy this file to ".env" and adjust as needed:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# This file contains ONLY non-secret, non-deployment-specific configuration.
# NEVER put real API keys, n8n credentials, invoice data, or internal
# service addresses here or in ".env" if you intend to commit it -- ".env"
# is git-ignored precisely so local secrets never end up in version control.
# The default "docker compose -f compose.dev.yml up --build" start works
# with NO values set below: Flow 1a (structured invoices, no AI) works with
# zero external credentials, and Flow 1b stays visible but inactive/
# unconfigured until you deliberately opt into local or cloud AI.

# --- Optional: local AI for Flow 1b ("PDF with local AI") ------------------
#
# Points Flow 1b's local extraction lane at a local, OpenAI-compatible
# chat-completions endpoint you already run yourself (e.g. LM Studio,
# Ollama with an OpenAI-compatible proxy, or any self-hosted equivalent).
# This project does NOT bundle, download, or run a model for you -- there is
# no local-AI Compose service. Point this at your own already-running
# endpoint. Leaving it unset means the local AI lane reports
# nicht_pruefbar/technical_review ("AI_LOCAL_PROVIDER_UNAVAILABLE") instead
# of silently falling back to cloud AI.
#
# Expect real hardware/download cost if you stand up a local multimodal
# model yourself: multi-GB weights and a GPU (or a slow CPU fallback) are
# typical for anything capable of reading an invoice PDF.
#
# LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:1234/v1
# LOCAL_LLM_MODEL=your-local-model-name

# Most local OpenAI-compatible vision endpoints (verified against LM
# Studio) reject a raw PDF passed as an image_url part and need an actual
# rendered image -- unlike Gemini's cloud API, which accepts the PDF
# directly. Run examples/n8n/scripts/pdf_render_service.py yourself
# (requires `pip install pymupdf`) and point this at it. Only needed for
# the local lane.
# LOCAL_PDF_RENDER_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8098

# --- Cloud AI for Flow 1b ("PDF with cloud AI") -----------------------------
#
# There is no cloud-AI variable here on purpose: the Gemini credential is
# selected inside the n8n UI itself (Credentials -> Google Gemini (PaLM)
# API), never via an environment variable or the browser. See
# examples/n8n/README.md for the exact steps. Flow 1b stays inactive until
# you select a real credential there.

# --- Flow 0 (mailbox intake) ------------------------------------------------
#
# Required before Flow 0 can call into TCMS at all. Generate one value and
# set it identically here and on TCMS's own NUXT_N8N_INGEST_SHARED_SECRET
# (tcms-framework/.env):
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# N8N_INGEST_SHARED_SECRET=

# This deployment's real TCMS organization id (the seed script that
# creates your organization prints it).
# UNTERNEHMEN_X_TCMS_ORGANIZATION_ID=

# Required before Flow 1b's cloud/local execution profile choice takes
# effect. No default is given on purpose, so an unset value fails closed
# rather than silently picking either provider -- select a real Google
# Gemini (PaLM) API credential in the n8n UI before setting this to
# cloud-gemini. "local-default" uses LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL/LOCAL_LLM_MODEL
# above.
# UNTERNEHMEN_X_AI_EXECUTION_PROFILE=cloud-gemini

# Required before Flow 0's two classification steps (body-level "has
# invoice?" and per-attachment is_invoice/is_issued_to_company) will run at
# all -- no default either way, fails closed to "...Profile Not Configured"
# if unset. "local-default" uses LOCAL_LLM_BASE_URL/LOCAL_LLM_MODEL above;
# "cloud-gemini" uses the Google Gemini (PaLM) API credential selected in
# the n8n UI (same credential Flow 1b's cloud lane uses) and sends real
# invoice/email content to the cloud provider -- only enable this for a
# tenant that has actually consented.
# UNTERNEHMEN_X_FLOW0_CLASSIFICATION_PROFILE=cloud-gemini

# Which real Gemini model every cloud-gemini call uses (Flow 0's two
# classifiers plus Flow 1b's own extraction node all read this same var).
# Defaults to gemini-3.6-flash if unset. A live-tested fallback pair exists
# if the current model's free-tier quota is exhausted: gemini-3.6-flash and
# gemini-3.5-flash both confirmed working; gemini-2.5-flash/gemini-2.5-pro
# are confirmed rejected ("no longer available to new users") despite still
# appearing in the API's own ListModels response -- don't retry those.
# UNTERNEHMEN_X_GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.6-flash

# No buyer-address variable here on purpose: Flow 0 fetches the
# organization's real buyer master data (name/address/countryCode) and
# controlProfileId directly from its published TCMS OrganizationBaseline at
# run time -- never duplicated into this file. Publish a baseline in TCMS
# before Flow 0 can process invoices for this organization; it fails
# closed until one exists.
